Z||000000||sloth85GT||08-18-2001||07:49 PM||||I'm SOOOOOOOOOOO happy, I'm going to Vancouver tomorrow at 2:30 PM, and we're driving there. No I'm not taking the Fiero, that's staying home. My girl and I are taking her Hyandai Accent. It's way better on gas and there's more room for a 24 hour drive. I'm just so stoked! <P>But there's a downside. I won't be able to chek PFF for a little while. Will be back on the 28th. Man is this gonna kick a$$!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Mach10||08-18-2001||08:10 PM||||I had just gotten back, and I took my Fiero. Best thing I ever did. That car just WHIPS through the mountains   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Take my advice: Take HWY-1 All the way through to Kamloops. Then take the Coquilhalla. Yeah, it'll cost $10 for the car, but the ride's better. Watch for construction between Golden and Revelstoke(?) I got hung up there, last time. Total drive-time, 23.5hrs. Beat that!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh, BTW, The mountain roads were infested with piggies. You don't want to be speeding there, anyway. <BR>Have fun, even though you're taking the (comparatively) lame car. You'd be shocked, amazed, and appalled at how much crap you can actually pack into a Fiero We had room for a 5'9/180lb male, a 6'3/260lb male, supplies, a tent, stove, cooler, and junkfood for both of us. And it was comfy. SO THERE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||sloth85GT||08-18-2001||11:42 PM||||I'll beat that time, even in my gf's  "lame car". And that was the route we were going to take too. Thanks for the advice.<P>Talk to you later Sean<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
